// stdlib/Transform.vein — VeinScript Standard Library : Vein.Transform
// Spatial state — general (used by desktop layout AND games). Position/Rotation/Scale as Shapes,
// Velocity with `folds sum` (many forces contribute), and a @Moved occurrence.
// Discover:  veinc symbols stdlib/Transform.vein

bundle Transform by Vein {

    publicator Spatial {
        shared("World/local position.")
        shape $Position { x: float, y: float, z: float }

        shared("Euler rotation (radians).")
        shape $Rotation { x: float, y: float, z: float }

        // WHERE AN IDENTITY ACTUALLY IS, after its parents. Written by the RUNTIME every phase, before
        // `settled` runs; a program reads it and never writes it. `$Position` stays what the PROGRAM
        // writes — local when the identity carries `*Vein.Core.Relations.$Parent`, absolute otherwise.
        //
        // Two shapes rather than composing `$Position` in place, because a composed position only the
        // renderer can see is worse than none: a collision pass subtracting one parented identity's
        // local from another's absolute does not fault and does not look wrong. The crate is DRAWN
        // where it belongs and fails to collide with what it is visibly touching.
        //
        // Present on EVERY positioned identity, parented or not — an unparented one's `$World` is its
        // `$Position`. Publishing it only for children would make every kit that reads it need a
        // fallback, and a conditional migration is where the silent bugs live.
        shared("Where an identity actually is, after its parents. Written by the runtime; a program reads it.")
        shape $World { x: float, y: float, z: float }

        shared("Non-uniform scale.")
        shape $Scale { x: float, y: float, z: float }

        shared("Velocity — many systems contribute, so each axis folds additively.")
        shape $Velocity {
            x: float folds sum
            y: float folds sum
            z: float folds sum
        }
    }

    publicator Motion {
        shared("An identity's position changed.")
        event @Moved { entity: Entity, x: float, y: float, z: float }
    }

    // No behaviour here — integrating $Position from $Velocity is the application's step, and its rules
    // (fixed vs variable step, clamping, sub-stepping) are its own. `$Velocity` folds sum precisely so
    // that many independent systems can contribute before that step runs.
}
